    {
      "type": "intro",
      "heading": "Why numbers first?",
      "body": "Numbers show up everywhere — prices, ages, phone numbers, times. Punjabi numbers one to ten are short, and once you know them you can already build real sentences like \"two brothers\" or \"one glass of water\".\n\nPunjabi has its own digits in the Gurmukhi script (੧, ੨, ੩…) but everyday writing often uses the digits you already know. Both are shown here."
    },
